# Command the go-to-waypoint controller to drive to a point.
#
# A service rather than a topic ON PURPOSE. A waypoint is a discrete operator
# decision that must be accepted or refused with a reason -- "the pose is not
# available", "that is 40 m away", "that frame is not the one I am driving in".
# A topic would let every one of those fail silently, and it would also give
# rm_dashboard a publisher, which it must never have.

# Frame the waypoint is expressed in: "map" or "odom". Must match the frame the
# controller is driving in; a mismatch is REFUSED rather than converted,
# because silently converting between a drifting frame and a corrected one
# changes where the robot is being sent without saying so.
string frame_id

float64 x
float64 y
---
bool accepted
string message
